This file describes the procedures to run the GMOS checkout test scripts.

* It is assumed you are in the main software tree directory (e.g. at ROE 
it is /net/alba/sw3/gmos/operational/gmos022/ for V22 software)

NOTE: If you change any setup read below for editting required
      Also note that all log files will be written into the logfiles 
      directory, given the same name as the test script with a .log 
      appended (eg. script name = gmTest.scr, then log will be called
      gmTest.log).  The log file created is overwritten each time 
      that test is run, but a backup copy of the form gmTest.log.date
      is saved.

      To use these tests on a running database with a different record
      prefix, it will only be necessary to edit the .config files in the
      "configFiles" sub-directory. The configFilesSim directory contains
      an example.

      IT IS IMPORTANT TO READ THE ASSUMPTIONS PRINTED AT THE START OF
      EACH TEST AND DECIDE WHETHER IT IS SAFE TO CONTINUE.

To run tests:

NOTE: To run these tests you need the "." and "./scripts" directories
      in your PATH.

NOTE: You have to be logged onto alba (or where the main software tree is) 
      as gmos and have the MK_access prompt (by typing 'gmosMK').

NOTE: Before running any checkout script it is assumed that either the
      software has been freshly rebooted or the device (or assembly) state
      has been reseted using the command <device>Reset (e.g. to checkout the
      translation stage x axis you need to first type 'xaxisReset').

(assemblyReset           Reset an assembly - used for testing the scripts only)
(deviceReset             Reset a device - used for testing the scripts only)


Pre Focal Plane Tests
---------------------

1.   cd gmoscc/test/ directory (should be where you found this file)

2a.  To do basic functionality tests one mask device at a time run 
     the "checkout" cshell script by typing checkout followed by 
     a <device> argument.  

     For example:

	rona 1 >  checkout grip
		or
	rona 1 >  checkout extractor
		or 
	rona 1 >  checkout release
		or 
	rona 1 >  checkout cassette

2b.  To test basic functionality for all four mask devices run 
     the "runTests" cshell script (use caution with this one)

2c.  To test basic functionality of the mask assembly:

	rona 1 >  checkout mask          *assumes an IFU is installed
		or 
                  checkout maskNoIfu     *assumes there is no IFU

2d.  To test basic functionality of the oiwfs assembly:

	rona 1 >  checkout wfs

2e.  To test mask portion of GMOS CC/IS ICD functionality:

	rona 1 >  checkout maskIcd      *assumes an IFU is installed

2f.  To do basic error checking tests on one mask device at a time:  

	rona 1 >  checkout extractorErr
		or 
	rona 1 >  checkout cassetteErr

	** Please note only extractorErr and cassetteErr are
	   available at this time.

2g.  To test basic error checking tests for all available pre focal plane devices run 
     the "runErrTests" cshell script

All of the above scripts take two optional arguments allowing 
you to add the popular "-debug" or "-auto" or both when you run
the test.

Post Focal Plane Tests
----------------------

3a.  To do basic functionality tests one filter device at a time run 
     the "checkout" cshell script by typing checkout followed by 
     a <device> argument.  

     For example:

	rona 1 >  checkout wheel1
		or
	rona 1 >  checkout wheel2

3b.  To test basic functionality of the filter assembly:

	rona 1 >  checkout filter

3c.  To do basic functionality tests one grating device at a time:

	rona 1 >  checkout turret
		or
	rona 1 >  checkout tiltA
		or
	rona 1 >  checkout tiltB
		or
	rona 1 >  checkout tiltC
		or
	rona 1 >  checkout tiltD
		or
	rona 1 >  checkout lifter

3d.  To test basic functionality of the grating assembly:

	rona 1 >  checkout grating

3e.  To test basic functionality of the translation axes one at a time:

	rona 1 >  checkout xaxis
		or
	rona 1 >  checkout yaxis
		or
	rona 1 >  checkout zaxis

3d.  To test basic functionality of the translation assembly:

	rona 1 >  checkout translation


